"TINY BASIC for the B8Script TTL Computer.";
"Statements: PRINT (or ?)  LET  IF..THEN  GOTO  GOSUB  RETURN  FOR..TO..STEP  NEXT";
"  INPUT  REM  END  STOP  LIST [n]  RUN  NEW  BYE.  Several per line with : between.";
"Expressions: + - * / ( ), relations = <> < > <= >= (true is 1), RND(n) ABS(n),";
"  variables A-Z and the array @(0..255). Numbers are 16-bit signed. A FOR body always";
"  runs once; NEXT V unwinds to V's loop. Lines are crunched as typed: keywords become";
"  one byte and blanks outside strings are dropped; LIST spells them out again.";
"Errors: WHAT? (syntax)  HOW? (no such line, divide by 0, RETURN or NEXT without";
"  GOSUB or FOR)  SORRY (out of memory or stack)  BREAK (Ctrl-C while running).";

"Memory. v is one block: v+0 variables A-Z, v+52 GOSUB stack (16 x c,t), v+116 FOR";
"  stack (8 x var,limit,step,c,t), v+196 line buffer, v+276 INPUT buffer, v+356 the @";
"  array, v+868 the expression operator stack, v+990 the keyword list's address,";
"  v+992 the BYE flag, v+994 the memory limit. z is the character table: 4 bytes per";
"  byte value c at z+4c: operator class, operand class, statement handler address.";
"  The program runs from p to e, where a sentinel line 32767 sits. Each line: number";
"  (2 bytes), length (1 byte, the whole line), text, CR. Keyword tokens are 80h + the";
"  place in the keyword list (PRINT 80h ... ABS 94h).";
"Globals: t text pointer, c current line, r running, q stop, x error, g GOSUB pointer,";
"  f FOR pointer, b FOR stack base, k break counter, s random seed, y operator stack";
"  pointer. Temporaries: Q h, U m n d, G m n o a, T m n o a l j i u w, I u a i j l,";
"  L j a o w i, P n, H a u, W a u, R a, E d i h j l. E is never re-entered: V calls it";
"  only for an @( target, and inside E @( is an operator.";

"B: the character at t.  C: (ch -- f) take ch if it's next.  D: (c -- f) digit?";
[B t@,]
[C B=:(t@1+t!0)]
[D 4*z@+1+,64=]
"N: read a number at t.  Z: (n -- 1..n) random.";
[N 0t@,D(10*t@,48-+t@1+t!t@,D)]
[Z s@25173*13849+:s! 16/%;4095& %/; 1+]

"Expressions: operator precedence, the operators on a stack in RAM, the operands on";
"  the data stack, so nesting costs no return-stack entries. Operator codes: 0 bottom";
"  1 ( 2 RND( 3 ABS( 4 @(  9-15 relation (8 + mask: 1 less, 2 equal, 4 greater)";
"  16 + 17 -  24 * 25 /  32 unary minus. Precedence is the code with its low 3 bits set.";
"  Operator classes in the table: those codes, 1 for ), 5 for : and 6 for CR (X uses";
"  those two; to E they end the expression). Operand classes: 64 digit,";
"  65 letter, or a prefix: 32 unary minus, 1 (, 10 RND, 11 ABS, 12 @ (8: a ( follows).";
"F: apply the operator on top of the operator stack (and pop it).";
[F y@1-:y!,
 :16=:(;;+ 1 0)\ :17=:(;;- 1 0)\ :24=:(;;* 1 0)\ :25=:(;;:0=(2x!0)/%; 1 0)\
 :32=:(;;0%- 1 0)\ :1=:(;; 1 0)\ :2=:(;;Z 1 0)\ :3=:(;;:0<(0%- 0) 1 0)\
 :4=:(;;255&2*v@356++@ 1 0)\ :8<:(;; 1 0)\
 7&{- :0<1&%:0=2&%0>4&||}&0=0=1&]
"E: evaluate an expression at t. Each pass: prefixes, an operand, then operators: a";
"  binary one is pushed after applying those of higher or equal precedence; a ) closes";
"  back to its mark (an unmatched one ends the expression, for @( targets).";
[E 0y@.y@1+y!
 1( t@,4*z@+1+,j! j@:64<&( j@39&y@.y@1+y! t@1+t! j@8&(t@1+t!0) t@,4*z@+1+,j! j@:64<&)
    0 j@64=(;N 0) j@65=(;t@,65- 2*v@+@ t@1+t! 0) j@64<(1x!0)
    0i! 1( t@,4*z@+,d!
       d@7>( t@1+t! d@16<( t@,4*z@+,:l! 7>l@16<&(d@l@|d! t@1+t! 0) 0)
             y@1-,7|d@7|<~(F y@1-,7|d@7|<~) d@y@.y@1+y! 1i! 0)
       d@1=( y@1-,7>(F y@1-,7>) 0) d@1=y@1-,0=~&h! h@(t@1+t!F 0) h@)
 i@)
 y@1-,(y@1-,8<(1x!0) F y@1-,) y@1-y!]
"V: the address of the variable or @(n) at t, or 0 if there is none.";
[V t@,4*z@+1+,:12=:(;;t@2+t! E 41C~(1x!0) 255&2*v@356++ 1 0)\
 65=:(;t@,65- 2*v@+ t@1+t! 1 0)\ 0]

"Program lines. Q: (n -- addr) first line numbered n or more.  U: (src dst n --) move.";
[Q h!p@ :@h@<( :2+,+ :@h@<)]
[U n!d!m! d@m@ - 0<:(n@(m@,d@.m@1+m!d@1+d!n@1-n!n@)0)
 ~(m@n@+1-m!d@n@+1-d! n@(m@,d@.m@1-m!d@1-d!n@1-n!n@)0)]
"I: enter the typed line at t (it starts with its number): delete, replace or insert.";
[I N u! u@1<u@32766>|(2x!0) x@\ t@a!
 a@:,13=~(1+:,13=~) a@- 4+ i! u@Q j!
 j@@u@=( j@2+,l! j@l@+ j@ e@4+j@l@+ - U e@l@- e! 0)
 i@4>( e@i@+4+32768^ v@994+@32768^<~(3x!0)
       x@0=( j@ j@i@+ e@4+j@ - U e@i@+e! u@j@! i@j@2+. a@ j@3+ i@3- U 0) 0)]
"J: (n --) GOTO line n.  L: LIST [n].  R: RUN.";
[J Q:@h@=:(;:c!3+t!1r! 1 0)\ ;2x!]
[L 1 B D(;N 0) Q j!
 j@@32767=~( j@@# 32' j@3+j! 32o!
   j@,13=~( j@,a!
     a@127>:( o@32=~o@58=~&o@40=~&(32'0) v@990+@w! a@128-i!
       i@( w@,32=~(w@1+w!w@,32=~) w@1+w! i@1-i! i@)
       w@,32=~(w@,'w@1+w!w@,32=~) j@1+,:40=%:58=%:13=%32=|||0=(32'0) 32o! 0)
     ~( a@'a@o! 0)
     j@1+j! j@,13=~)
   j@1+j! 13'10'
 j@@32767=~)]
[R 0a!1(0v@a@+!a@2+:a!52<) v@52+g! b@f! p@c! c@@1+0<(1q!0) c@3+t!1r!]

"Statements. P PRINT, Y INPUT, H FOR, W NEXT. S runs one statement: the handler for";
"  the character at t, from the table (keyword tokens, letters, digits, : and CR).";
[P 1n! B4*z@+,:4>%7<&0=(
   B34=:(t@1+t! t@,:34=~%13=~&(t@,'t@1+t!t@,:34=~%13=~&) t@,34=(t@1+t!0) 0)~(E x@0=(#0) x@(;0) 0)
   0 59C(;-1 0)44C(;9'-1 0) :0=n! B4*z@+,:4>%7<&0=&)
 n@x@0=&(13'10' 0)]
[Y B34=(t@1+t! t@,:34=~%13=~&(t@,'t@1+t!t@,:34=~%13=~&) t@1+t! 59C;44C; 0)
 1( V:0=(1x!0):("? "$ v@276+:G T t@{v@276+t!E}t! %! 0 0); 44C x@0=&)]
[H V:0=(1x!0) u! 61C~(1x!0) E u@!
 f@a! a@b@ - 0>( a@10-a! a@@u@=(a@f!0) a@b@ - 0>)
 145C~(1x!0) E 1 146C(;E 0) f@b@80+=(3x!0)
 f@4+! f@2+! u@f@! c@f@6+! t@f@8+! f@10+f!]
[W V u! u@( f@b@ - 0> f@10-@u@=~&( f@10-f! f@b@ - 0> f@10-@u@=~&) 0)
 f@b@=(2x!0) x@\ f@10- a!
 a@@:@a@4+@+:{%!} a@2+@ - a@4+@0<(0%- 0) 0>~
 :(a@6+@c! a@8+@t! 0)~(a@f! 0)]
[S B 4*z@+2+@{]
"T: (buf --) crunch a typed line in place: keywords to tokens, blanks out (not in";
"  strings or after REM), ? to PRINT.";
[T :m!n! 0o!
 1( m@,a!
   a@13=~(
     o@:( a@n@.n@1+n! m@1+m! a@34=(0o!0) 0)
     ~( a@34=:( a@n@.n@1+n! m@1+m! -1o! 0)
        ~( a@32=:( m@1+m! 0)
           ~( 0l! a@63=(128l! m@1+m! 0)
              l@0=( v@990+@j! 128i!
                1( m@u!j@w! w@,:u@,=%32=~&(w@1+w!u@1+u!w@,:u@,=%32=~&)
                   w@,32=:(u@m!i@l!0)~(j@,32=~(j@1+j!j@,32=~)j@1+j!i@1+i!0)
                 l@0=j@,34=~&) 0)
              l@0=~:( l@n@.n@1+n! 0)~( a@n@.n@1+n! m@1+m! 0)
              l@136=( m@,13=~( m@,n@.n@1+n!m@1+m! m@,13=~) 0)
            0) 0) 0)
   0)
 a@13=~)
 13n@.]

"X: run statements from t until the line ends (immediate) or the program stops.";
[X 0q! 1( S
 x@q@|0=( B4*z@+,l! l@5=(t@1+t!0)
   l@6=( r@( t@1+:c! @1+0<(1q!0r!0) q@0=( c@3+t! k@1+:k!15&0=(1?3=(4x!0)0) 0) 0)
         r@0=(1q!0) 0) 0)
 x@q@|0=)]
"O: report an error and reset the stacks.  G: (buf --) read a line with echo.";
[O x@( x@1=("WHAT?"$0) x@2=("HOW?"$0) x@3=("SORRY"$0) x@4=("BREAK"$0)
   r@(" IN "$c@@#0) 13'10' 0x!0r! v@52+g! b@f! v@868+y! 0)]
[G m!0n!0o! 1( 0?a!
   a@8=a@127=|( n@(n@1-n! m@n@+,34=(o@~o!0) 8'32'8' 0) 0)
   a@31>a@127<&n@72<&( a@34=(o@~o!0) o@0=a@96>&a@123<&(a@32-a!0)
     a@m@n@+. n@1+n! a@' 0)
 a@13=~) 13m@n@+. 13'10']
"M: the command loop. S stores a typed line that starts with a number; others run.";
[M 0v@992+! 1( 62' v@196+:G T v@196+t! 0r! X O v@992+@0=)]

